[h2]0.9.0[/h2]
[h3]Steel decks on legs[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]New: Steel deck 3×3 and 5×5 on legs[/b], 1, 2, 3 or 4 layers high (Paths → Steel structures). The deck appears that high above the spot you point at, with a steel column under each corner that reaches down to the first support: the ground (also under water), a platform or a flat roof. Every leg finds its own height, so the deck stays level over slopes, terraces and water.
[*][b]One click places everything:[/b] the preview shows the exact columns that will be built, and builders put up the columns first, then the deck. Legs reach up to 12 layers; longer legs are two stacked columns.
[*]If a leg runs into a building or finds no support, the preview turns red and says why. The tool panel shows the extra cost of the columns for the spot under the cursor.
[*]The separate steel columns and decks are still there for building by hand.
[/list]
